MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per AUFTRAG-anchor-scheduler.md (MMC-OS docs), based on the findings in
DIAGNOSE-turbo-anchor.md: there was no batcher/cron/timer — the 9 pending
batches waited forever for manual POST /api/chain/submit calls.

S.1 src/anchor/scheduler.ts: interval worker (ANCHOR_SCHEDULER_INTERVAL_MS,
default 15 min, 0 = off). Submits via loopback self-call to the EXISTING
/api/chain/submit route — no second signing/wallet code path. Read-only
(no wallet key) is a deliberate state: log only, no error. Max 1 batch per
tick (gas conservation). Backoff: max 3 attempts per batch, then status
"failed" in DB + MANUELLE_KARTE log + audit entry — no silent retry loop.
Graceful shutdown waits for an in-flight tick (K8s rollout safe).

S.2 GET /api/chain/status: new mandatory field mode "anchoring"|"read-only"
(derived from walletAddress), scheduler metrics object (laeuft, letzterTick,
verarbeiteteBatches, fehlversuche, fehlerhafteBatches), existing fields
unchanged for compatibility.

S.3 network consistency guard: on startup and each tick, compares the
configured network vs. where the wallet actually holds funds
(eth_getBalance on both Base networks). On mismatch: WARN log +
netzwerkHinweis field in chain/status — would have surfaced the current
Sepolia-config/Mainnet-wallet conflict in seconds.

chain-db: additive helpers getPendingBatchIds() + markBatchFailed().
typecheck (tsc --noEmit) green; apps/service has no existing test suite.

